  "title": "Double Bonus Application in updateToSMNFT() Inflates Voting Power and Corrupts Global Balance Tracking",
  "body": "## Summary\n\nThe VotingEscrow contract manages vote-escrowed tokens with special Super Massive NFT (smNFT) functionality that provides bonus voting power. The `updateToSMNFT()` function converts regular locked positions to smNFTs, which should apply a one-time bonus while maintaining accurate balance tracking. This conversion is critical for the voting mechanism and affects user voting power calculations across the entire protocol.\n\n```solidity\nfunction updateToSMNFT (uint _tokenId, IVotingEscrow.LockedBalance memory _locked) internal {\n    _locked.isPermanent = true;\n    _locked.isSMNFT = true;\n    uint _amount = uint(int256(_locked.amount));  // Gets potentially bonused amount\n    smNFTBalance += _amount;  // Adds wrong amount to global balance\n    _locked.end = 0;\n    uint _value = uint256(uint128(_locked.amount));\n    _locked.amount = int128(int256(_value + calculate_sm_nft_bonus(_value)));  // Double bonus\n    _checkpoint(_tokenId, locked[_tokenId], _locked);\n    locked[_tokenId] = _locked;\n    assert(_black.burn(_value));  // Burns wrong amount\n}\n```\n\nThe function incorrectly assumes that `_locked.amount` contains only the base token amount without any existing bonuses. However, analysis of other contract functions reveals that `_locked.amount` may already include bonuses from previous operations:\n\nEvidence from `_deposit_for()`:\n```solidity\nif(old_locked.isSMNFT) {\n    _locked.amount += int128(int256(_value + calculate_sm_nft_bonus(_value)));\n}\n```\n\nEvidence from `merge()` function which carefully handles bonus tracking:\n```solidity\nif (!_locked0.isSMNFT) {\n    // If source wasn't SMNFT, add bonus for its amount\n    smNFTBalance += value0;  // Only adds base amount\n} else {\n    // Both already include their bonuses\n    newLockedTo.amount = _locked1.amount + _locked0.amount;\n}\n```\n\nThe contract provides `calculate_original_sm_nft_amount()` specifically to extract base amounts from bonused values, but `updateToSMNFT()` fails to use it.\n\n## Impact\nThis vulnerability creates multiple severe issues affecting the core token economics:\n\nThe `smNFTBalance` global variable becomes inflated because it receives bonused amounts instead of base amounts. This corrupts voting power calculations since `smNFTBalance` is used in `totalSupplyAtT()` and other critical functions.\n\nUsers converting existing smNFTs or previously bonused positions receive additional unintended bonuses, creating unfair voting power advantages and potential governance manipulation.\n\nThe function burns the wrong amount of tokens, leading to supply accounting errors that cascade through the entire protocol's token economics.\n\nSophisticated users could potentially trigger multiple conversions to accumulate excess bonuses, gaining disproportionate voting power and protocol influence.\n\n## Remediation\n\n```solidity\nfunction updateToSMNFT(uint _tokenId, IVotingEscrow.LockedBalance memory _locked) internal {\n    _locked.isPermanent = true;\n    _locked.isSMNFT = true;\n    \n    // Extract original base amount to prevent double bonus\n    uint _originalAmount = calculate_original_sm_nft_amount(uint(int256(_locked.amount)));\n    \n    smNFTBalance += _originalAmount;  // Add only base amount to global balance\n    _locked.end = 0;\n    \n    // Apply single bonus to base amount\n    _locked.amount = int128(int256(_originalAmount + calculate_sm_nft_bonus(_originalAmount)));\n    \n    _checkpoint(_tokenId, locked[_tokenId], _locked);\n    locked[_tokenId] = _locked;\n    \n    assert(_black.burn(_originalAmount));  // Burn only base amount\n}\n```\n\nThis bug directly affects core token economics, voting power calculations, and protocol governance. The state corruption and potential for economic exploitation make this a critical issue requiring immediate attention.",
